        ":question/problem": "What is the value of ${\\int }_{3}^{21}\\frac{1}{x}{log}_{7}\u2061(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u={log}_{7}\u2061(\\frac{x}{3}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20617}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20617}\\,\u27f9\\,\\operatorname{ln}\u20617\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $21$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{21}\\frac{1}{x}{log}_{7}\u2061(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{21}{log}_{7}\u2061(\\frac{x}{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u20617\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20617{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20617\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u20617}{2}\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u20617}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
